        "kernel_unified_attention_2d"
      ],
      "platforms": [
        "gfx950"
      ],
      "kernel_class": "attention_decode",
      "regime": "decode",
      "key": "paged bf16 KV attention decode in Triton on gfx950, where each KV tile is loaded exactly once per workgroup",
      "lifecycle": "active",
      "layer": "learned",
      "cost": "L1",
      "type": "lever",
      "confidence": "★★",
      "effect": "conditioned hint is worth -11.9% of the weighted speedup if reverted; per-case, dropping the hint gains +21% to +27% on the long-trip wide-head bf16 case (about 79%->84% of achievable bandwidth) but the 1-trip narrow-head bf16 case prefers keeping it by ~7%, while a 1-trip fp8-KV case prefers dropping it by ~2.3%",
      "attempts": 4,
      "losses": 2,
      "confirms_cited": 0,
      "confirms_blind": 0,
      "blind": false,
      "verified_on": "2026-08-17",
      "last_seen": "2026-08-17",
      "lever": "Treat the hint as a host-selected predicate rather than a constant: the wrapper picks allocate-in-L1 when the tile loop is long OR the KV element is sub-2-byte, and the bypass hint otherwise.",
      "apply": "Thread the KV cache's own element size into the launch-config helper (the element_size already in scope is usually the query's), then pass the modifier as a kernel argument; no math changes, so parity is free.",
      "verify": "Median of paired ratios, arms interleaved in one lock session, per case; expect opposite signs on long-trip and 1-trip cases, so a geomean alone cannot tell you the predicate is right.",
      "pitfall": "the rule was first keyed on bytes per tile -> two cases carry identical bytes and identical trip count yet want opposite policies, so that feature is degenerate -> key on element width, because the paged gather issues one address per element and L1 absorbs requests, not bytes\na flip of the cache policy invalidated the tile and split-count sweeps measured underneath it -> the same knob that was 20-48% worse before became a 3.1% win in the other direction after -> re-open the launch-config sweeps after any memory-policy change, and vice versa",
      "caution": "Also verify the two tensors separately before assuming a per-tensor policy is two levers: here the sensitivity was almost entirely on the value stream and a mixed policy landed at the worse uniform arm.",
      "source": "GEAK 12h per-kernel time-budget campaign, run mi355x_vllm_triton_unified_attention-bmk7-12h, 2026-08-17, rounds 3/4/14/15, director-validated accepted, correctness PASS"
    },
    {
      "title": "Unclamp the KV tile from the page size, then de-rate it by head width",
      "description": "Paged attention wrappers that clamp the KV tile to the page size and floor the split count over-subscribe the CUs; unclamping with a head de-rate is ~1.37x.",
      "keywords": [
        "launch-config",
        "tile-size",
